<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Multiplying two surds and simplifying into the form k*sqrt(m)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: Write <code>40*sqrt(91)</code> to represent \(40\sqrt{91}\).)</i></p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ {@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}} \]</p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Multiply the numbers outside the square roots</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@a@} \times {@b@} = {@ab@}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Multiply the square roots using \(\sqrt{x} \times \sqrt{y} = \sqrt{x \times y}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \sqrt{{@n@}} \times \sqrt{{@m@}} = \sqrt{{@n@} \times {@m@}} = \sqrt{{@nm@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Combine the outside number and the simplified square root</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}} = {@ab@} \times \sqrt{{@nm@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
